      "content": "That's a good start. But those feel like pretty standard talking points. My student is going to face some really smart opponents who have prepared counter-arguments for those exact points—like how automation might make work scarce anyway, or how UBI could actually boost the economy through increased consumer spending.\n\nCan you dig deeper? Give me the arguments that actually make the Pro side look unprepared or even intellectually dishonest. I need the \"knockout\" punches that don't just argue the economics, but really dismantle the whole philosophy behind it.",
